  // 原本此位是「緩和（détente）指哪一種狀態」，與題庫既有一條（標作 hard）
  // 概念、正解及干擾項結構重複，等於製造模板複本，故換走。改考柏林的位置 ——
  // 一個地圖層面的基本事實，卻正是理解柏林封鎖與柏林圍牆的前提，題庫從未問過。
  { t: 'cold',
    q: ['二戰之後德國被分為東西兩部分。柏林這座城市位於哪一邊的境內？',
      'After the Second World War Germany was divided into east and west. Within which side did the city of Berlin lie?'],
    o: [['整座柏林位於東德境內，市內再分為東西柏林',
      'the whole of Berlin lay inside East Germany, and the city itself was then divided into east and west'],
      ['整座柏林位於西德境內，市內再分為東西柏林',
      'the whole of Berlin lay inside West Germany, and the city itself was then divided into east and west'],
      ['柏林剛好橫跨東西德的邊界，一半屬一方',
      'Berlin straddled the border exactly, with half on each side'],
      ['柏林由蘇聯單獨管治，並不分為東西兩部分',
      'Berlin was administered by the Soviet Union alone and was not divided at all']],
    e: ['柏林雖然位於蘇聯佔領區（即其後的東德）之內，卻由四國分區佔領，故西柏林成為東德境內的一塊「飛地」，四面被東德包圍。認清這一點，柏林封鎖與柏林圍牆才講得通：蘇聯只需切斷陸路通道即可圍困西柏林，西方唯有靠空運補給；而圍牆之所以要環繞整個西柏林而非沿東西德邊界修築，原因亦在於此。把柏林誤置於西德境內，其後的整段敘述都會失去邏輯。',
      'Berlin lay inside the Soviet occupation zone, which became East Germany, yet the city itself was occupied in sectors by the four powers, so West Berlin formed an enclave surrounded on every side by East German territory. Grasping this makes the Berlin Blockade and the Berlin Wall intelligible: the Soviet Union needed only to cut the land routes to besiege West Berlin, leaving the Western powers to supply it by air; and the Wall had to encircle the whole of West Berlin rather than run along the inner-German border for the same reason. Placing Berlin inside West Germany leaves the entire subsequent narrative without its logic.'],
  },

